  "understanding": "The focused helpers synchronously calculate deletion bounds and delegate inclusive deletion to the selected LogStore. Normal compaction retains an index window and never requests deletion beyond the supplied snapshot index. removeOldLogs instead uses the store's observed last index with zero trailing retention; its restore callers and monotonic-store selection checks remain unread. The built-in memory store and cache adapter have distinct completion, synchronization, and durability semantics.",
